   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "Let me find the decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{7} = 0.142857142857142857\\ldots$$\n\nThe decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$ has a repeating pattern of period 6: $142857$.\n\nThe digits to the right of the decimal point are:\n$$1, 4, 2, 8, 5, 7, 1, 4, 2, 8, 5, 7, 1, 4, 2, 8, 5, 7, \\ldots$$\n\nTo find the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit, I divide 2007 by the period length 6:\n\n$$2007 \\div 6 = 334 \\text{ remainder } 3$$\n\nSo the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit corresponds to the 3rd position in the repeating block $142857$, which is:\n\n$$\\boxed{2}$$",
